WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.667
-I've never played
that game faster

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:04.701
with a more confident person
in my entire lifetime.

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:08.100
-I wanted more.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.667
-No, I'll tell you
what happened.

00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:11.434
You're just excited about
the World Cup,

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:13.467
'cause France won.

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:15.901
-Yes!
-Oh, my gosh.

00:00:15.901 --> 00:00:18.868
-Yes. France won today.
-Yeah, but you were so excited.

00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:20.968
But you love the World Cup.
-I love the World Cup.

00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:25.901
It's a very important time,
every four years, for my family.

00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:28.834
-Yes. And --
But who do you root for?

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:30.901
You root for --
-Well, for Mexico.

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:31.968
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:33.801
-Of course.

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:37.100
Until they get disqualified.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:40.334
Then I go for France.
-Yeah.

00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:46.400
-Because it's very important
to keep a good marriage.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.801
-But can you tell me
what you were saying earlier?

00:00:48.801 --> 00:00:50.267
'Cause there was
someone watching the game

00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:51.467
with you at your house.

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:54.767
-We were watching the --
We loved the pranks.

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:56.033
-Yes, pranks are fun.
Yeah, they're fun.

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:58.968
-I think if you're Mexican,
it's in your genes.

00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:00.234
-Oh, really?
-Yes.

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:01.868
-Yeah.
-And --

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:03.601
-But this is a good thing.
You can play this at home.

00:01:03.601 --> 00:01:05.701
-Yeah. We were
all watching the game,

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:07.667
the Mexico game.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:10.534
And there was a friend
who wanted to go to the bathroom

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:13.234
for a long time but didn't
want to miss anything.

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:14.667
-Yeah.

00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:17.701
-And, finally, he built up --
He couldn't take it anymore.

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:19.868
And he went into the bathroom.

00:01:19.868 --> 00:01:24.534
And we all waited a little bit
for him to put his pants down,

00:01:24.534 --> 00:01:26.033
and then we all screamed,
"Goal!"

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:28.901
-"Goal!"

00:01:28.901 --> 00:01:30.534
He came running out of
the bathroom.

00:01:30.534 --> 00:01:33.801
"What's going on?!"
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:33.801 --> 00:01:36.167
Yes, of course.
-That's such a good bit.

00:01:36.167 --> 00:01:38.801
-Yes.
-I love that. I'm gonna do that.

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:41.133
Well, happy holidays.
What do you do for the holidays?

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:43.701
Do you spend it here?
Where do you spend it?

00:01:43.701 --> 00:01:46.434
-I do fake holidays,

00:01:46.434 --> 00:01:52.267
because we have to have
Christmas with my family.

00:01:52.267 --> 00:01:55.234
and then a Christmas
with François' family.

00:01:55.234 --> 00:01:56.400
-Yeah.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.300
-But -- And then we have our own

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:00.434
little family
to have a Christmas.

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:01.634
But I'm not Santa Claus

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:04.067
that can be in many places
at the same time.

00:02:04.067 --> 00:02:05.434
-No, yeah. Yeah, he's magic.

00:02:05.434 --> 00:02:09.601
-So we pretend,
like on the 21st or the 22nd,

00:02:09.601 --> 00:02:11.234
that it's Christmas.

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:13.801
And we do it with my family.
And then we pretend again --

00:02:13.801 --> 00:02:15.767
-You just wake up and you go,
"It's Christmas"?

00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:18.901
-Yeah, "Oh, it's Christmas Eve."

00:02:18.901 --> 00:02:20.767
And we do the cooking.

00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:22.701
So, we live
Christmas three days.

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:26.167
-Does everyone know
that it's fake Christmas?

00:02:26.167 --> 00:02:29.567
-Everybody knows,
but everybody's a good actor.

00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:30.634
And the Christmas spirit --

00:02:30.634 --> 00:02:32.300
-In your house,
it could be a prank.

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.534
You'd be like,
"Merry Chr-- Just kidding."

00:02:34.534 --> 00:02:37.801
-You know, when it gets tricky
is in the nacimiento,

00:02:37.801 --> 00:02:39.634
you know,
where you put the baby?

00:02:39.634 --> 00:02:40.767
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:42.067
-Sometimes, we have
some conversations like,

00:02:42.067 --> 00:02:43.234
"Put the baby.

00:02:43.234 --> 00:02:45.767
"It's not Christmas."
"Just put the baby."

00:02:45.767 --> 00:02:49.968
-Yeah. Can you explain to me
what's happening

00:02:49.968 --> 00:02:51.167
in this photo, because --

00:02:51.167 --> 00:02:52.567
-Oh, yes.
-Okay.

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:55.834
-That's my owl.
-Yes, I know that.

00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:58.167
So, that's a real owl.
-That's a real owl.

00:02:58.167 --> 00:03:02.367
-Yes.
-She loves Christmas.

00:03:02.367 --> 00:03:04.767
She, however,
hates the World Cup.

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:06.167
-She does not like
the World Cup?

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:08.501
-No, because
she doesn't understand why

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:11.300
we're screaming
and the house is shaking.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.434
You know?
She doesn't get soccer.

00:03:13.434 --> 00:03:15.300
She loves Christmas,
the Christmas tree.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:16.400
She destroys the little things.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:17.567
-You're like,
"France is winning,"

00:03:17.567 --> 00:03:19.033
and the owl's like, "Who, who?"

00:03:19.033 --> 00:03:20.534
-Yes, exactly.

00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:23.534
-You can take that joke.
Take it. I can't turn it off.

00:03:23.534 --> 00:03:25.734
Can't turn it off.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:25.734 --> 00:03:27.334
I can't stop it.
I can't stop it.

00:03:27.334 --> 00:03:28.734
It's terrible.

00:03:28.734 --> 00:03:31.067
Bad jokes all over my house.

00:03:31.067 --> 00:03:33.300
But the owl -- Does the owl go
in the tree at all?

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:36.100
-Yes, the owl goes --
What do you mean go in the tree?

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:39.667
Like, go in the bathroom --

00:03:39.667 --> 00:03:41.133
-No, not go to the bathroom.

00:03:41.133 --> 00:03:44.734
Do you put -- Does the owl go
in, like, as an ornament?

00:03:44.734 --> 00:03:47.834
-I actually have another owl
that is a fake owl

00:03:47.834 --> 00:03:49.734
that is an ornament.

00:03:49.734 --> 00:03:51.133
And I have to say --

00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:53.167
-What happens when this owl --
-She gets really confused.

00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:54.534
She tries to,
like, play and stuff,

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:58.767
but the other owl
is just really stuck-up.

00:03:58.767 --> 00:04:01.133
Then, she starts checking
all the balls and stuff.

00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:02.300
-Yeah.
-You know?

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.367
I have a Tour Eiffel,
she likes that one.

00:04:04.367 --> 00:04:07.067
-She loves it.
-Yeah, she loves it.

00:04:07.067 --> 00:04:09.334
-I love that you always
have fun like this.

00:04:09.334 --> 00:04:11.767
-She scares everybody, though.
-The owl does?

00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:17.067
-Yeah, because, you know --
How fun is it to scare people?

00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:19.300
I love it. I love it.
-I do not love it.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:21.434
-I love -- You don't love
scaring people?

00:04:21.434 --> 00:04:23.300
-I do not like
anyone scaring me

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:24.767
and I don't like scaring anyone.

00:04:24.767 --> 00:04:27.067
-But, Jimmy,
the anticipation of the face --

00:04:27.067 --> 00:04:28.834
-It feels like
you're going to scare me now.

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:32.133
-I start laughing.
You know, I enjoy it so much.

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:33.367
And then --
-I just heard a noise.

00:04:33.367 --> 00:04:36.300
-It's just imagining
the reactions.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.234
-Stop talking about it.
I'm getting scared.

00:04:38.234 --> 00:04:40.334
No one's getting scared tonight.
-I love it.

00:04:40.334 --> 00:04:41.467
-No, we're going to
talk about --

00:04:41.467 --> 00:04:42.901
We're going to talk about
"Puss in Boots."

00:04:42.901 --> 00:04:44.400
-Yes, let's talk about
"Puss in Boots."

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:47.601
-"Puss in Boots: The Last Wish."
By the way, it's phenomenal.

00:04:47.601 --> 00:04:49.434
-It's really good, guys.
-I loved the other ones.

00:04:49.434 --> 00:04:51.267
This one's my favorite one.
-Sometimes, I lie to you.

00:04:51.267 --> 00:04:52.534
I say, "Oh, it's really good.
Go see it."

00:04:52.534 --> 00:04:54.067
No, this one's for real.
-This one's fantastic.

00:04:54.067 --> 00:04:56.267
It has a...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:56.267 --> 00:04:59.734
96% rating on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:04:59.734 --> 00:05:01.100
And my girls watched it,

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.634
and they were just like,
"This is the best movie ever."

00:05:02.634 --> 00:05:05.133
-And the best part,
it's good for the entire family.

00:05:05.133 --> 00:05:07.267
-It was funny jokes.
It was good songs.

00:05:07.267 --> 00:05:08.534
-Yeah.
-It was great.

00:05:08.534 --> 00:05:11.400
-Even the teenagers,
which are so hard to please,

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:12.634
are going to like this one.

00:05:12.634 --> 00:05:14.801
-It got a
Critics' Choice nomination

00:05:14.801 --> 00:05:15.834
and a Golden Globe nomination.

00:05:15.834 --> 00:05:16.901
Congratulations.
-So far.

00:05:16.901 --> 00:05:19.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:19.133 --> 00:05:20.734
Great cast also.
-Not bad.

00:05:20.734 --> 00:05:23.501
Fanta-- Antonio Banderas.
-Wonderful.

00:05:23.501 --> 00:05:25.400
-You guys together
are just fantastic.

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:27.968
I mean, with this,
the whole idea of this one is,

00:05:27.968 --> 00:05:29.734
he's down to his last life.

00:05:29.734 --> 00:05:31.033
He's -- 'Cause Puss --

00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:34.434
-You know, cats have nine,
but he's got one left.

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:38.067
-Yeah. He's lived so much that
he's down to his last life.

00:05:38.067 --> 00:05:40.834
And it's like, when that
happens, what do you do?

00:05:40.834 --> 00:05:42.701
You've got to kind of
think about life, eh?

00:05:42.701 --> 00:05:44.367
-Well, that's what's
wonderful about the film,

00:05:44.367 --> 00:05:46.367
that it's really philosophical.

00:05:46.367 --> 00:05:49.367
But it's does, like,
what the first "Shrek" did,

00:05:49.367 --> 00:05:53.534
that the humor is for the kids,
take it one way,

00:05:53.534 --> 00:05:54.801
the adults another way.

00:05:54.801 --> 00:05:55.968
And this talks about a lot of

00:05:55.968 --> 00:05:58.501
really interesting
things in life,

00:05:58.501 --> 00:06:01.434
and the kids see it one way, but
for us, it's very interesting.

00:06:01.434 --> 00:06:02.968
-They did
a fantastic job with it.

00:06:02.968 --> 00:06:05.000
And you did fantastic, as well.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:08.434
Here is Salma Hayek Pinault in
"Puss in Boots: The Last Wish."

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:09.501
Take a look.

00:06:09.501 --> 00:06:12.567
-Kitty,
may I please see the map?

00:06:12.567 --> 00:06:13.934
-No.
-Seriously?!

00:06:13.934 --> 00:06:16.234
You won't let me hold it
for even one minute?

00:06:16.234 --> 00:06:18.133
-Nope. Not even for one second.

00:06:18.133 --> 00:06:23.834
-Come on, Kitty.
You've got to trust me.

00:06:23.834 --> 00:06:26.167
-Wait. W-What's going on
with his eyes?

00:06:26.167 --> 00:06:28.467
Oh, they're getting bigger.

00:06:28.467 --> 00:06:30.868
Oh, Kitty!

00:06:30.868 --> 00:06:33.133
You've got to trust him.
Look at those eyes.

00:06:33.133 --> 00:06:35.400
-Really? You call that cute?

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:37.667
-[ Gasps ] Oh, look at her!

00:06:37.667 --> 00:06:38.801
[ Gasps ]

00:06:38.801 --> 00:06:41.601
Those guys are
even bigger than yours.

00:06:41.601 --> 00:06:42.968
Do whatever she wants, Puss.

00:06:42.968 --> 00:06:44.501
Wait a second.

00:06:44.501 --> 00:06:46.100
So poofy!

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:48.467
No! With the paws?

00:06:48.467 --> 00:06:49.968
Come on!
[ Gasps ]

00:06:49.968 --> 00:06:51.868
With the hat?

00:06:51.868 --> 00:06:54.701
It's all...so...cute!

00:06:54.701 --> 00:06:58.634
Cuteness overload!

00:06:58.634 --> 00:07:00.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:00.434 --> 00:07:02.501
-Salma Hayek Pinault, everybody.

00:07:02.501 --> 00:07:07.033
"Puss in Boots: The Last Wish"
is in theaters December 21st.

00:07:07.033 --> 00:07:09.467
We'll be right back with
Wiz Khalifa. Stick around.

